@alejandraalonsorojas keeps busy. As a designer and new mother of two, she splits her time between her studio and apartment in New York’s Soho neighborhood. When she’s not visiting family in her native Madrid, she’s likely unplugging on Shelter Island.
For the uninitiated, the sleepy town near the eastern end of Long Island is only accessible by ferry, making it feel both local and blissfully removed—a favorite escape for Manhattanites. There’s a reason Jonathan Adler, Rickie De Sole, and others spend part of their summers there. “Shelter Island is best enjoyed by staying either at a waterfront resort, perfect for families looking for space and amenities, or at a charming boutique inn for a quieter, more intimate escape,” Rojas tells ELLE.
At the link in bio, read Rojas’s full guide to Shelter Island

@kyliejenner has had a busy 2026. It's easy, then, to forget that it's only been two years since the launch of the mogul's first fragrance, Cosmic. Now comes an expansion to @kyliecosmetics's scents: the Mood Stones Fragrance Collection.
Featuring three distinct fragrances, this collection was designed to offer a scent for every mood. “I wanted Mood Stones to be an embodiment of my versatility, and for people to be able to honor how they feel in the moment,” Jenner tells ELLE.
To celebrate the launch, we chatted with Jenner about the new Mood Stones collection, astrology, and her favorite scent to wear courtside. Read the full interview at the link in bio.

